## DO NOT REPEAT
- Do NOT accept internal consistency (HUD/labels/transform agreeing) as proof of orientation — must use screen-space projection (ndc signs / projected screen coords).
- Do NOT reference THREE in codex-browser eval (not a global).
- Do NOT read/copy code from other projects (clean room).
- codex-browser eval does NOT await Promises/async — (async()=>{...})() returns {}. Use synchronous calls + shell `sleep` between separate codex-browser invocations so the rAF loop advances >=1 frame (camera re-syncs each frame). The old setInterval step-driver pattern was UNRELIABLE (callbacks never fired) — avoid it.
- Camera re-syncs only on the next animation frame after setYaw/setPlayerPosition/setZombiePosition — always wait >=1 frame (shell sleep ~0.3-1s) before reading __AGENT_STATE__ or firing.
- Pure-lateral projection is NaN (point in near-plane) — expected math, NOT a bug; prove A/D via forward+diagonal points or the camera right vector.
- Never call camera.updateMatrixWorld() (or any transform recompute) from eval-side helpers between frames — it clobbers the live camera transform set by syncCamera() each frame.
- Pointer lock can't be engaged headlessly; hide #start to screenshot in-game view.
- fire() within the ~0.09s cooldown window is a no-op — always wait >=0.25s between fire() calls in test sequences.
